      "message": "[warning] Line 734: 🟡 `fitToSize()` is applied to any payload larger than 16 KiB, but there is no hard upper bound before parsing/re-serializing. After removing the old 64k guard in `JamiAccount::sendTrustRequest`, a very large payload can now force expensive parsing/allocation in `toMap()`/`toString()`. Add an absolute size cap (e.g., reject/clear payload above a conservative limit) before calling `fitToSize()` to avoid local DoS via oversized trust-request payloads.",
